\begin{lemma}\label{lemma1}
    Let $M\in \mathbb{SR}^{m\times m}.$ Then $\vec(M) = \mathcal{J}^m_{S}\vec_{S}(M),$
    where $$\mathcal{J}^m_{S}=\bmatrix{\mathcal{J}^{(1)}_{S}& \mathcal{J}^{(2)}_{S} & \cdots &\mathcal{J}^{(m)}_{S}}\in \R^{m^2\times \frac{m(m+1)}{2}},$$  $\mathcal{J}^{(i)}_S\in \R^{m\times (m-i+1)}$  are defined by
  {\footnotesize  \begin{align*}
\mathcal{J}^{(1)}_{S}=\bmatrix{e_1^{m}& e_2^{m}&e_3^{m} & \cdots&e_{m-1}^{m}& e_m^{m}\\
    0 &e_1^{m} &0& \cdots &\cdots&0\\
