\textbf{Linear layer.}
This layer in the GPT2 model transforms the embedding dimension of the input data $\mathbf{X}$ from $N_e$ to $N_d$ via a linear transformation.
Formally, this transformation is done through a matrix multiplication and an addition of a bias over unchanged dimensions: $\bY = \bW\bX \mathop{+.} \mathbf{b}$, where $\bY$ is of size $N_d \times N_s \times N_b$, $\bW$ is of size $N_d \times N_e$ and $+.$ denotes the summation of the same data over unchanged dimension.
Tile-based implementation of this layer is also straightforward and based on the multiplications and additions of elementary tiles.


