\textbf{Layer normalization layer.}
Normalization layers are designed to improve stability of the training process and avoid gradient vanishing/exploding phenomena.
Since our primary focus is the transformer-based models, we consider the Layer Normalization layer~\cite{ba2016layer}.
This type of normalization shows superior performance for transformer models over alternative normalization layers~\cite{xiong2020layer}.
The tile-based implementation of this layer consists of three steps: mean and variance of every tile accumulation, normalization of every tile and scaling with an addition of bias.
