    We first determine conditions on the index of refraction, $n$, such that there are no resonances close to the real axis.
    \begin{theorem}
    \label{t:simple}
     Suppose that $\Omega_{\inner}$ is non-trapping and $n\in C^\infty(\overline{\Omega}_{\inner};(0,\infty))$ satisfies $n|_{\partial\Omega}<1$. Then for all $M>0$ there is $C>0$ such that 
     $$
     \mathcal{R}(n,\Omega_{\inner})\cap \{ |\Re \lambda|>C\}\subset \{\Im \lambda<-M\}.
     $$
    \end{theorem}
