    We next show that there is $z$ with $\Im z>0$ such that $(P-z^2):\mathcal{D}(P)\to L^2$  and $(P-\overline{z^2}):\mathcal{D}(P)\to L^2$ are surjective. This then implies that $P-\Re (z^2)$ and hence also $P$ is self-adjoint. 

