\end{cases}
\end{align*}
{and we recall that extreme (large magnitude) \( z \)-scores correspond to low \( p \)-values, indicating statistically \textit{atypical} configurations, while small \( z \)-scores and high \( p \)-values reflect \textit{typical} behavior.}
