\begin{abstract}
We develop a unified second-order parameterized complexity theory for spaces of integrable functions.
This generalizes the well-established case of
%second-order parameterized complexity theory for spaces of 
continuous functions.
Specifically we prove the mutual linear equivalence of three
natural parameterizations of the space $\Lrm{p}$ of $p$-integrable complex functions on the real unit interval:
(binary) $\Lrm{p}$-modulus, rate of convergence of Fourier series, 
and rate of approximation by step functions.
\keywords{Integrable Functions \and Complexity Theory \and Second-Order Parameterization \and Approximation Theory}
\end{abstract}

