\subsection{Bochner-Riesz Means}
\label{ss:BochnerRiesz}

Recall that Fourier coefficients $\hat f_K$
from Equation~\ref{e:Fourier} are well-defined for every $f\in\ELL{p}(\IT)$,
$p\geq1$ fixed. However the asociated Fourier series
according to Equation~\ref{e:Fourier} may fail to converge.
Instead, consider the sequence of Bochner-Riesz Means

\begin{equation}
\label{e:BochnerRiesz}
\Bochner_{L}^{(\gamma)}f\,(t) \;:=\; 
\sum\nolimits_{|K|\leq L} \left(1-\frac{|K|^2}{L^2}\right)^{\gamma} \cdot \widehat{f}_K \cdot \exp(2\pi i K t) 
\end{equation}
for fixed $\gamma\geq0$ and with $L$ running over $\IN$.
Note that $\gamma=0$ recovers Equation~\ref{e:Fourier},
while for $\gamma>0$ the coefficient to $\exp(2\pi i K t)$ 
now depends on both $K$ and $L$.

The Bochner-Riesz \emph{Conjecture} is concerned with the `critical' index $\gamma$, 
in dependence on $p$ and on the dimension (see Subsection~\ref{ss:Dimension}),
beyond which $\big(\Bochner_{L}^{(\gamma)}f\big)_L$ converges to $f$ in $p$-norm.

