\begin{lemma}
\label{basic_large}
Let $M$ be a basic $0,1$ matrix of size $n \times m$ with $\Rreal(M) = d$.
Then for any $s,t$ such that $d \leq s \leq n, d \leq t \leq m$, there exists a basic sub-matrix $A$ of $M$ of size $s \times t$ such that $\Rreal(A) = d$.
