%of Euclidean one. %geometry. 
%We show that the examples found in isotropic geometry %the solution of the simplified problem 
%can then be used as a good initialization to construct Euclidean ones %solve the original problem 
%via numerical optimization. This approach has been (implicitly) used since as early as %the work 
