Our final application deals with the computation of asymptotic gridshells with
constant node angle, in particular those that approximate a given boundary curve;
see Fig.~\ref{fig:CRPC1} and Section~\ref{sec:CRPC}.
Geometrically, this amounts to the computation of a surface with a constant ratio
of principal curvatures. In isotropic geometry, the problem is simplified
by a novel approximation of such surfaces using complex analysis.


Details on the optimization are provided in Section~\ref{sec:optimization}
and their performance, choice of parameters, and a discussion of results
and future work form the content of Section~\ref{sec:conclusion}. 











