We already know what to do whenever we face a hard Euclidean problem: consider its isotropic analog, that is, the surfaces with a constant \emph{isotropic} angle $\gamma$ between asymptotic curves. %As usual, there are many analogous properties, but the expressions become simpler. This allowed us to characterize several classes of isotropic CRPC surfaces including rotational and translational ones \cite{Yorov-etal}. 
