the surface normal is orthogonal to the curve binormal at each vertex $f_1, \cdots, f_{k-1}$.  
Orthogonality is expressed using the inner product, but instead of the Euclidean one, we employ the special inner product \(\langle \cdot, \cdot \rangle_\varepsilon\).  
