\textbf{Fairness.}
To enforce smoothness of $C$, we apply a soft fairness constraint. If \( f_i \) is not connected to the boundary, we require $f_i$ to
%it must 
be close to the midpoint of \( f_{i-1} f_{i+1} \):  
\begin{equation}\label{constr:fairness}  
2f_i - f_{i-1} - f_{i+1} \approx 0.  
\end{equation}  
Otherwise, \( f_{i-1}, f_i, \) and \( f_{i+1} \) are required to be close to collinear:  
\begin{equation}\label{constr:fairness1}  
\frac{f_i - f_{i-1}}{\|f_i - f_{i-1}\|} - \frac{f_{i+1} - f_{i}}{\|f_{i+1} - f_{i}\|} \approx 0.  
\end{equation}  
The fairness energy \( E^{C}_f \) is the sum of the squared left sides of either~\eqref{constr:fairness} or~\eqref{constr:fairness1} over all $0< i <k$.  


